      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could we check the required additional subpools against `max_subpools - n_subpools` before allocating? The overflow check can accept requests that exceed the cache’s actual capacity, so the growth loop eventually calls `clib_panic()` instead of returning `-1`. For example, with default geometry and one thread, `n_elts \u003d UINT32_MAX - 256` passes this check but exceeds capacity after batch headroom.",
      "revId": "b2bf79cdf78330d3f2db2260112460377ad14f28",
      "serverId": "6d2eb258-4fe2-443e-8a38-ca81da23d4c2"
    },
